From 92542af16e936e0339f2215e7ce458dae1d70e17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:27:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] Render the keyboard in RGB565 when the compositor offers
 it

On a 240x320 RGB565 panel an ARGB8888 buffer doubles the memory of the
double-buffered keyboard surface and forces the compositor to blend and
convert every repaint. The surface now uses WL_SHM_FORMAT_RGB565 with
CAIRO_FORMAT_RGB16_565 when wl_shm.format advertises it, otherwise
XRGB8888, otherwise ARGB8888 as before. --format
auto|rgb565|xrgb8888|argb8888 forces a choice for testing.

Formats without alpha draw every colour opaque, so --alpha and --bg-alpha
are ignored there (documented in --help and the man page) and the
baseplate gets square corners instead of black ones. The popup surface
stays ARGB8888 because it is mostly transparent.

All buffer-size arithmetic lives in drw_buffer_geometry(), which pads rows
to 4 bytes and rejects sizes that do not fit the int32 wl_shm and cairo
use. A drwsurf without a wl_shm now backs onto plain memory, which lets
tests/test-draw.c draw a layer through kbd_draw_layout() for each format
and check key, baseplate, label and highlight pixels without a compositor.
Upstream-Status: Pending
